    "description": "The Orthophotomosaic SWISSIMAGE (Background) is a composition of digital color aerial images of Switzerland and surroundings. The orthophotos of the neighboring countries come from SPOT 5 satellite images (Airbus Defence and Space) taken in 2004 and 2005 with a ground resolution of 5 m. An orthophoto is an aerial image in which the distortions created by the camera and the relief are corrected. The layer is used as base map in the swiss federal geoportal. It is also available as WMS and WMTS geoservices. Once a year, a copy of the WMTS tile pyramid is made available for download in JPEG format and in the Web Mercator coordinate system (EPSG:3857) up to zoom level/tile matrix 18 (0.5 m resolution).",
